# Fixed-reference Benefit-of-the-Doubt index on Alkire-Foster censored headcounts

Reproduction package for the article *Pesos endógenos e referência fixa na mensuração territorial
da pobreza multidimensional: evidência para o Brasil, 1991 a 2022* (Brandão, Mariano and Rebelatto). Release 1.0.0 accompanies manuscript v4 (26 October 2026). The main application uses the 2010 and 2022 censuses; the historical extension requires the additional 1991 and 2000 SPSS samples described below.

## Method in short

1. **Identification (Alkire-Foster).** Twelve deprivation indicators in four dimensions, equal
   weights 1/12, poverty cut-off k = 1/3 (IPM-Brasil definitions; income line of one quarter of
   each year's minimum wage). Person-level indicators (education, work) are
   assigned to the household when at least one resident is deprived; every resident shares the
   household profile.
2. **Profiles.** For each UF and year, the censored headcount of each indicator: the share of
   persons who are poor and deprived in that indicator. M0 is their mean.
3. **Score.** Benefit of the Doubt with unit input against a fixed reference B, the 27 UF profiles
   of 2010: S(h) = max w'h subject to Bw <= 1, w >= 0 and w_j >= (tau/12) sum(w). The restriction
   does not depend on the evaluated profile, so the admissible set of weights is the same in every
   evaluation. tau = 0 is the unrestricted model; tau = 1 gives S = M0 / max M0 of the reference.
   Main specification: tau = 0.5.
4. **Aggregation.** Population-weighted mean of the UF scores (regions and Brazil).

## Requirements

R 4.2 or later with `data.table`, `lpSolve`, `rDEA` (GLPK, second solver) and `Benchmarking`
(check of the unrestricted model); the command-line tools `unzip` and `awk`. For the full solver validation install both `rDEA` and `Benchmarking`. The optional historical extension also requires `haven` and `tidyselect`. The validated environment uses R 4.5.3 on macOS; full raw-data reproduction needs substantial memory and disk space. Shell-based extraction requires a Unix-like environment (Linux, macOS or WSL).

## Data

| Census | Source | Files |
|---|---|---|
| 2010 | IBGE, Censo Demográfico 2010, Resultados Gerais da Amostra, microdados. <https://ftp.ibge.gov.br/Censos/Censo_Demografico_2010/Resultados_Gerais_da_Amostra/Microdados/> | one zip per UF (São Paulo in two parts) and `Documentacao.zip` |
| 2022 | IBGE, Censo Demográfico 2022, microdados da amostra de acesso público. <https://ftp.ibge.gov.br/Censos/Censo_Demografico_2022/Microdados_e_Areas_de_Ponderacao/Microdados_de_acesso_Publico/csv/> | `Todas_as_UFs.zip` |

Stage 01 downloads the files that are missing and records their SHA-256 (`output/inputs_sha256.csv`).
IBGE releases corrections to the microdata; a different release may change the results slightly.
Paths can be set with `BOD_CENSUS2010_DIR`, `BOD_CENSUS2022_ZIP`, `BOD_WORK_DIR` and `BOD_OUTPUT_DIR`.

## Running

```
Rscript run_all.R            # all stages and the tests
Rscript run_all.R 05 06 07   # only the listed stages (list each stage)
Rscript tests/check_results.R
```

| Stage | Script | What it does | Main outputs |
|---|---|---|---|
| 01 | `01_download.R` | downloads missing files; checksums | `inputs_sha256.csv` |
| 02 | `02_build_census2010.R` | households of 2010 with the 12 indicators, from the fixed-width files; checks person records against V0401 | `work/households_2010.rds`, `base_2010_counts.csv` |
| 03 | `03_build_census2022.R` | households of 2022 with the same indicators | `work/households_2022.rds`, `base_2022_counts.csv` |
| 04 | `04_af_profiles.R` | AF identification; censored headcounts, H, A and M0 by UF, region and Brazil; robustness profiles | `af/` |
| 05 | `05_scores.R` | scores against the fixed 2010 reference and against each year's own reference, for every tau; aggregates; weights | `scores/` |
| 06 | `06_audit.R` | independent solvers; interference under moving and fixed references; monotonicity in the profile and at household level; componentwise within-UF worsening | `audit/` |
| 07 | `07_robustness.R` | real income line, harmonized school delay, four dimensions, eleven indicators, suppressed ages; pooled, normative and leave-one-out references; rank ranges over tau; dominant indicator with its range over optimal solutions; bootstrap | `robustness/` |
| 08 | `08_numerical_example.R` | numerical example of the article | `numerical_example/` |
| 09 | `09_series_1991_2022.R` | optional: 1991 and 2000 Census samples (SPSS files given by `BOD_CENSUS1991_SAV` and `BOD_CENSUS2000_SAV`; needs `haven`), same indicators, scores against the fixed 2010 reference and each year's own reference; skipped when the files are not set | `series/` |
| 10 | `10_figure.R` | Figure 1 of the article | `figure/Figura_1.png` |
| 11 | `11_manifest.R` | parameters, session information, output checksums | `outputs_sha256.csv` |

Indicator definitions and Census variable codes: `docs/indicators.md`.

